=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Classify unordered tetrads using the given parental cross.
- Distinguish linked and unlinked gene pairs.
- Calculate map distances from tetrad counts.
- Solve each pair and determine three-gene order.
- Map a gene relative to its centromere using ordered asci.

=== layout: definitions

# Unordered Tetrad Classes

@body

- Parental Ditype (PD): four spores with only the two parental allele combinations.
- Nonparental Ditype (NPD): four spores with only the two nonparental allele combinations.
- Tetratype (TT): one spore of each of the four allele combinations.

