=== layout: reference

# Unordered Tetrad Mapping Reference

@body

- PD and NPD are defined by the given parental combinations.
- Linked genes: PD is much greater than NPD.
- Unlinked genes: PD and NPD are approximately equal.
- TT and NPD below are counts; N is the total number of tetrads.

$$
D = \frac{\frac{1}{2}TT + 3NPD}{N} \times 100 \;\mathrm{cM}
$$

