=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- Use the cross to identify parental combinations.
- Classify all four spores for the selected pair.
- Test linkage before calculating a map distance.
- Reclassify the tetrads when you change gene pairs.
- Reversed gene orders describe the same map.
- Ordered asci let you estimate a gene's distance from its centromere.

